NAME
       killall - send a signal to all processes with a given name

SYNOPSIS
       killall [-s SIGNAL | -SIGNAL] NAME...

DESCRIPTION
       killall sends a signal (SIGTERM by default) to every process whose
       command name is exactly NAME. It says "NAME: no process found" and
       exits with 1 when there is none. Normal users can only signal their
       own processes.

       pkill does the same with a pattern instead of an exact name, and can
       pick processes by user (pkill -u).

       killall is in the psmisc package.

OPTIONS
       -s SIGNAL, -SIGNAL
              Send this signal instead, for example -9 or -HUP.

EXAMPLES
           killall sleep
           killall -9 dd

SEE ALSO
       kill(1), pkill(1), pgrep(1), ps(1)
